# S5-S6: press when ahead, be harder to hit

The first score gain outside the noise

Unit 1, talk 5

---

## S5: a distance controller (DIST-1)

- 1.20 always stood off at 650 px
- Now Hadur keeps the last 100 shots of each side as rolling hit rates
- While ours leads theirs by 5 points beyond the margin, it comes in 25 px
- While theirs leads by 5 points, it goes back out
- A stranger starts at 650 px

---

## S5: the bench moved the floor

| Closest distance | Effect on sample bots |
|---|---|
| 150 px | Their head-on guns took 0.4 to 2 points of share |
| 300 px | A little still lost |
| **400 px** | Every share back at its S4 level |

The floor went from 150 to **400 px**. The bench, not intuition, set it.

---

## S5: power and the endgame

- **Full power (POW-1, POW-2):** against a gun the profile rates T0, or when we clearly out-hit them, fire power 3. Landing it refunds 9 energy.
- **Finish and ram (END-1, END-2):** when the enemy is under 16 energy and we have over 40, close to 150 px. A disabled enemy is rammed.
- Neither applies at 12 energy or less.

---

## S5 result

- Shadow **46.3% ± 4.5** cold, **48.5% ± 2.5** warm (S4 re-run: 45.5% and 44.0%)
- Sample bots: rounds end sooner (Crazy's rounds 459 to 399 ticks) without losing share
- Against Shadow the controller mostly stays out
- Warm beat cold for the first time, but the intervals still overlap

---

## S6: go after the other half of the damage

Shadow's hits on Hadur.

- **Bullet shadows (MOVE-1):** Hadur follows its own bullets in flight and works out which enemy firing angles they would block. The surf treats those angles as safer.
- A **tick budget (TIME-1, TIME-2)** sheds work after a slow tick or a skipped turn

---

## S6: checking the geometry against the engine

- Check: did every enemy bullet that ours destroyed fall inside a computed shadow?
- Result: **927 of 927** in the cold bench
- It took three rounds of fixes against the truth logs: **35%, then 83%, then 100%**
- The engine moves bullets in a random order each tick, so some shadows are certain and some count as half

---

## S6: what lost, and what did not show

- **Go-to surfing** lost its A/B: 51.8% ± 5.1 against 54.8% ± 3.7 for three options. Kept only in reserve.
- **Movement changes when hit (MOVE-2)** fired 8 times warm, but the score was the same with it off (54.6% against 55.2%).

Ideas that do not win the A/B do not become the default.

---

## S6 result: the first real move

| Shadow, cold | S5 | S6 |
|---|---|---|
| Score share | 46.3% | **57.4% ± 5.0** |
| Their hit rate on Hadur | 9.9% | **7.9%** |
| Rounds won | 99 / 175 | **125 / 175** |

Samples still 875 of 875. Skipped turns 72, not the zero the gate wanted.

---

## What it taught us

- Attack the other half of the exchange: fewer hits taken is as good as more hits landed
- Check a geometric idea against ground truth until it reaches 100%
- Run the A/B. Two clever ideas lost theirs.
- Report the gate you missed (zero skipped turns). It became the next work.

---

